The fixed orientation is `F=degree 108`, `G=degree 72`. It is the opposite of
the historical lower-case `(f,g)` order in some source passages. The
Tschirnhausen tower is

```text
h3 = P,                                  deg_y 9,   top P=y^2(y-x)^7
h2 = P^4 + C2 P^2 + C3 P + C4,          deg_y 36
F  = h2^3 + A2 h2 + A3,                 deg_y 108
G  = h2^2 + B1 h2 + B2.                 deg_y 72
```

Set `z=w-1`,

```text
K3(t,w)=t^9 h3(t^-1,w/t),
K2(t,w)=t^36 h2(t^-1,w/t).
```

At the major `D2` node, `t=s^4`, `z=pi*s^6`; hence the weight is
`4r+6q`, or primitive weight `W=2r+3q`. At `D1`, `s=e^2`, so
`t=e^8`, `z=e^12(1+Pi*e)`. This is the charged §3 convention
(`g108-minor-classification...md:320-325`). Replacing it by `4r+5q` would
identify the major flag coordinate with the later physical minor series; that
is precisely the flag/place/series conflation barred by FALLACY-v2. The two
maps are declared separately below.

