codex
With a free linear coefficient, the raw residual no longer kills under `c!=0` alone, but it forces the quadratic discriminant to vanish. Since the sourced split branch is `[1,1]`, the right localization is the discriminant, so I’m replaying that weakened-gauge system in Singular.
exec
/bin/bash -lc "timeout 3000 bash -lc 'cat > box/g108gate-20260903/linear-free-cutoff43.sing <<\"EOF\"
ring R=0,(jet1,jet2,b,c,ZD),dp;
poly r60=-jet2"'^2;
poly r70=2*jet1''^2*jet2;
poly r71=-2*jet2;
poly r80=-c-jet1''^4+9*jet1*jet2''^2;
poly r81=b+2*jet1''^2;
poly L=ZD*(b''^2+4*c)-1;
ideal I=r60,r70,r71,r80,r81,L;
ideal S=std(I);
print("DIM"); dim(S);
print("SIZE"); size(S);
print("NF1"); reduce(1,S);
quit;
EOF
